abstract: |
  causalgeo is a package for concurrent geo holdouts that reports bundle
  lift, uses impression paths for a model-assisted channel split, and
  refuses channel estimates that the design cannot distinguish. Each cell
  turns a bundle of channels off in a group of markets and compares those
  markets with business-as-usual controls. One bundled test estimates that
  bundle's total lift.
  It does not estimate how many sales each channel's impressions were
  worth. Splitting that one total requires a sales-per-impression weight
  the user already has. The package does not calculate that weight.
  A channel response is reported when different cells separate the
  channels. Channels whose impressions are copies stay blank.
